  std::vector<SceneFieldChange> canonicalChanges;
  std::optional<FullSnapshotReference> fullSnapshot;
};
```

`SceneFieldValue` is a closed tagged value union, never `void*`, callback, document reference, native handle, or mutable span. It contains final immutable values for node local TRS/matrix mode; local visibility; material scalar/vector/alpha/double-sided/extension fields; material texture/sampler/UV binding; primitive material/variant binding; camera parameters/attachment; light type/color/intensity/range/cones/attachment; hierarchy parent and attachment; and topology create/delete metadata. Full snapshot references own or reference immutable MGIF content by verified digest.

`ImmutableSceneSnapshotRef` is an owning immutable value or a hash-addressed ID in an MGIF-owned content store whose lifetime covers deferred apply. It is not a pointer into `GltfDocument`, `SceneProjection`, or a caller stack. The stable-ID remap is complete for Compact/Merge/topology changes: an absent old ID means create, an absent new ID means delete, and both present means identity remap. Its canonical order is the same stable-key order used for field changes.

For a `Create`, `beforeValue` is absent and `afterValue` is complete; for `Update`, both are present; for `Delete`, `beforeValue` is complete and `afterValue` is absent. The document mutation token is required for `DocumentMutation` and its source chain and absent for a pure activation/root-state transition. Optional active-scene IDs represent the explicit no-active-scene state, not an invalid fabricated ID.

`FullRebuildReason` is a stable enum containing at least `SceneSwitch`, `GlobalMerge`, `Compact`, `StructuralTopology`, `GeometrySchema`, `TextureSchema`, `AccelerationStructureTopology`, `MappingMismatch`, `MissedRevision`, `DeviceRecovery`, `UnsupportedIncrementalCapability`, and `ExplicitCallerRequest`.

Envelope rules are exact:

- Document mutation: one unbatched source step has target revision = base + 1. A coalesced request may span several revisions only when `sourceMutations` contains every adjacent step from the header base to target, with matching intermediate document digests and no duplicate/missing revision. Scene-activation epoch is unchanged; root serial changes only if the committed operation freezes/replaces root external state.
- Scene activation: document revision and root serial are unchanged; activation epoch is base + 1; active scene changes.
- Scene root state: document revision and activation epoch are unchanged; active scene is unchanged; root serial is base + 1.
- Full snapshot: target revision may advance by more than one, but complete immutable target projection and all target digests are mandatory.
- Every checked increment rejects overflow before publication.

P5-10 adds a typed activation API while retaining any required compatibility wrapper:

```cpp
