On integration failure caused by a leaf contract defect, P5-90 stops without editing the leaf. The corresponding leaf owner receives a separately ordered retry; P5-90 then rebinds the new report/hashes. On G5 failure, G5 remains read-only and the same owner-routing rule applies. A fresh G5 run is required after every repair.

### 10.6 Renderer runtime retry

A rejected stale/gap/mapping/device delta has zero RHI side effects. The caller requests a new full snapshot anchored to current fences. A failed candidate retains the old active generation and may retry only from a freshly validated request; it cannot replay orphan command buffers or reuse a partially staged descriptor generation. Device loss increments generation and invalidates all old requests.

## 11. Final acceptance and non-claims

Gate P5 can pass only when all of the following are independently demonstrated:

- next committable frame document/projection/renderer digests match exactly;
- continuous edits have zero full rebuild, geometry upload, texture upload, device idle, and partial publication;
- hierarchy/topology/full snapshot paths are candidate-staged, atomic, rollback-safe, deferred-retired, and Vulkan Validation/synchronization clean;
- every fence mismatch and injected fault preserves the old active generation and exact fences/digests;
- public/direct/wrapper/transitive N11 findings are zero with zero approved exceptions;
- Debug and Release evidence is complete, Android desktop editor isolation holds, and Metal is reported honestly.

